Session branching retains an unlimited session continuation
examples/sessions/linear_if.links
filemode : true
args : --fresco --path=lib/stdlib --set=show_quantifiers=true --set=hide_fresh_type_vars=false
stdout : fun : forall a::(Unl,Session).modal [effect_0$Wild] ((?(Bool).!(Int).a::(Unl,Session)) -> ())

Execute session example reccalc
examples/sessions/reccalc.links
filemode : true
stdout : 84 : Int

Execute session example sim-calc
examples/sessions/sim-calc.links
filemode : true
stdout : 42 : Int

Execute session example atm
examples/sessions/atm.links
filemode : true
stdout : (16, 0, Just(128)) : (Int, Int, [|Just:Int|Nothing|])

Encoded choice callbacks retain the caller handler
open import Choice; effect E { Read : () => Int; } var ap = (new() : AP(Choice({A:End}))); var child = spawn { close(sel_A(request(ap))) }; handle <E> (off(accept(ap),fun(x) { switch(x) { case A(s) -> {close(s); do Read} } })) { case x -> x case <Read => k> -> k(42) }
args : --fresco --path=examples/sessions:lib/stdlib
stdout : 42 : Int

Encoded choice callbacks retain contextual results
open import Choice; effect E { Read : () => Int; } var ap = (new() : AP(Choice({A:End}))); var child = spawn { close(sel_A(request(ap))) }; handle <E> ({ var action=off(accept(ap),fun(x) {switch(x) {case A(s) -> {close(s);fun(){do Read}}}}); action() }) { case x -> x case <Read => k> -> k(42) }
args : --fresco --path=examples/sessions:lib/stdlib
stdout : 42 : Int

Linear-list callbacks visit both channels under the caller handler
open import FrescoLinearList; effect E { Step : () => (); } var ap = (new() : AP(End)); var child = spawn { close(accept(ap)); close(accept(ap)) }; var channels = (LinCons(request(ap),LinCons(request(ap),LinNil)) : LinList(End)); var channels = handle <E> (linMap(fun(c) { do Step; c },channels)) {   case channels -> channels   case <Step => k> -> {print("step");k(())} }; sig drain : modal [Wild] ((LinList(End)) -> Int) fun drain(channels) {   switch(channels) {     case LinNil -> 42     case LinCons(c,channels) -> {close(c);drain(channels)}   } } drain(channels)
args : --fresco --path=examples/sessions/chatserver:lib/stdlib
stdout : stepstep42 : Int

Encoded selection retains non-session alternatives in its residual row
open import Choice; fun(e:(!(modal [] [|A:End|B:Int|]).End)) { close(sel_A(e)) }
args : --fresco --path=examples/sessions:lib/stdlib --set=typecheck_only=true

Execute the finite process-encoding example
examples/sessions/pi.links
filemode : true
stdout : () : ()

Compile recursive duality definitions without invoking them
examples/sessions/forkbomb.links
filemode : true
stdout : () : ()

Execute the successful two-factor session
examples/sessions/two-factor.links
filemode : true
stdout : "secret data" : String

State cells retain read write and swap behaviour
open import State; { var cell = newCell(40); var before = get(cell); put(cell,41); var previous = swap(cell,42); (before,previous,get(cell))  }
args : --fresco --path=examples/sessions:lib/stdlib
stdout : (40, 41, 42) : (Int, Int, Int)

State swaps transfer linear absolute payloads
open import State; typename Once = modal [] (() -@ Int); var cell = ~newCell[Once]((linfun(){40}:Once)); var before = ~swap[Once](cell,(linfun(){2}:Once)); var previous = ~swap[Once](cell,(linfun(){0}:Once)); before()+previous()
args : --fresco --path=examples/sessions:lib/stdlib
stdout : 42 : Int

State get rejects a linear payload
open import State; typename Once = modal [] (() -@ Int); ~get[Once]
args : --fresco --path=examples/sessions:lib/stdlib
exit : 1
stderr : @.*Type does not satisfy its kind or usage requirement.*In expression: ~get\[Once\].*

State put rejects a linear payload
open import State; typename Once = modal [] (() -@ Int); ~put[Once]
args : --fresco --path=examples/sessions:lib/stdlib
exit : 1
stderr : @.*Type does not satisfy its kind or usage requirement.*In expression: ~put\[Once\].*

State cells reject contextual function payloads
open import State; newCell(fun(){42})
args : --fresco --path=examples/sessions:lib/stdlib
exit : 1
stderr : @.*instantiation constraints.*In expression: newCell.*

Process callbacks can install their own handler
open import Pi; effect E {Read:()=>();} newChannel(fun(c){handle <E> (do Read) {case x->x case <Read => k> -> k(())};stop})()
args : --fresco --path=examples/sessions:lib/stdlib
stdout : () : ()

Process callbacks cannot use the caller handler
open import Pi; effect E { Read:()=>(); } handle <E> (newChannel(fun(c){do Read;stop})()) {case x->x case <Read => k> -> k(())}
args : --fresco --path=examples/sessions:lib/stdlib
exit : 1
stderr : @.*The operation's effect is absent from the ambient context.*In expression: do Read.*

